WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:06.390
You type www dot example dot org
into a browser and press enter.

2
00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:10.490
Your request hops across the
internet, from router to router.

3
00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:12.710
But look at the address on the packet.

4
00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:19.330
No name, just a number:
203 dot 0 dot 113 dot 25.

5
00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:21.890
Routers only use numbers like this.

6
00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:24.510
So where did the name you typed go?

7
00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:27.410
In this mission, you'll
take a web address apart,

8
00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:28.970
piece by piece.

9
00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:33.830
You'll see that every device on the
internet is found by its own IP address.

10
00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:36.510
And you'll watch a web
server send a page back,

11
00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:38.370
for your browser to render.

12
00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:42.480
Your mission: work out how a
typed web address finds its site.
